---
id: org.dxos.plugin.lighthouse
name: LighthousePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A Composer plugin that is lighthouse's web UI. Lighthouse (an agent that searches the web and keeps what it
finds as an RDF graph) runs outside Composer, as its workspace daemon, and is reached through its API
(`lighthouse-api`, routes under `/v1`). The plugin adds a **Research** object to a space: a goal handed to a
lighthouse search session. Its article follows plugin-commerce's Search: the goal, budget, search engines and Run
with the session's steering thread on the left, a ranked masonry of what the session found on the right, and the
selected result's detail in the companion. The person steers the agent, votes on results and reads facets of a
result on demand; what they keep (the agent's picks and the results they star) is copied into the space, so it is
shared with the space's members and outlives the lighthouse workspace.

Lighthouse's own code stays in its repository; everything this plugin knows about lighthouse's HTTP routes lives
in one module, `LighthouseClient`.

## Extensions

| Term        | URI                          |
| ----------- | ---------------------------- |
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`      |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0` |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`   |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`  |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`      |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Where things live

| What                                                             | Where                                        |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Sessions, trajectories, the graph, the rating model, extensions | Lighthouse (its workspace), via the API      |
| The Research: goal, budget preset, engines, connection, run      | ECHO, in the space                           |
| Picks and starred results, as immutable `Finding`s               | ECHO, the Research's feed                    |
| Stars                                                            | ECHO, the Research's tag index               |
| Votes                                                            | Lighthouse (the session's feedback)          |
| The connection (server URL and API token)                        | ECHO, a plugin-connector Connection          |

Everything else the article shows (every result, the live thread, extension sections, the rating model) is
read live from the API and not copied.

## Types

```mdl
type Research
  desc: >
    A goal handed to a lighthouse search session. Links to the session by run id on one lighthouse
    connection; holds what was kept as an append-only feed of Findings.
  fields:
    name?:       string
    goal:        string
    budget?:     quick | standard | deep    # a preset; the session gets its numbers (BUDGETS)
    engines?:    string[]                   # lighthouse engine ids; none lets the agent choose
    connection?: Ref<Connection>            # the lighthouse server it runs on
    run?:        string                     # the lighthouse session; set once it starts
    feed:        Ref<Feed>                  # immutable Finding entries (SetParent)
    tags:        Ref<TagIndex>              # the starred flag per Finding (SetParent)
    lastRunAt?:  string                     # ISO 8601
  annotations:
    icon: ph--binoculars--regular
    hue: amber
    label: name
```

```mdl
type Finding
  desc: >
    One result copied out of lighthouse into the space: the entity's identity and facts at the time it was
    kept, with where they came from. Immutable; the feed is the Research's history of what was kept.
  fields:
    iri:        string                      # the lighthouse subject
    title:      string
    url?:       string
    types:      string[]                    # CURIEs, e.g. schema:CafeOrCoffeeShop
    images:     string[]
    properties: Record<string, Value[]>     # CURIE → values, as lighthouse returns them
    provenance: FindingSource[]
    score?:     number                      # the rating score when kept
    why?:       string                      # the agent's reason, for a pick
    keptBy:     pick | person
    keptAt:     string                      # ISO 8601
  annotations:
    icon: ph--push-pin--regular
    hue: amber
    label: title
```

```mdl
type FindingSource
  fields:
    extractor: string                       # id@version
    source?:   string                       # the page or API it read
    at:        string
```

## Components

```mdl
component ResearchArticle
  desc: >
    Article surface for a Research, in plugin-commerce's SearchArticle shape. Left pane: the goal and budget
    preset (a schema form), the search engines as checkboxes (from listEngines), Run, the session's meters
    (pages, cost, time, status), and under them the session's trajectory as the assistant ChatThread
    (ResearchThread) with a composer for follow-ups. Right pane: a masonry of ResultCards, the report's picks
    first, then the rest ranked by the session's rating model with the person's overrides. The toolbar toggles
    All results and Findings, and offers Stop while a turn runs. Selecting a tile opens ResultArticle in the
    companion.
  props:
    research: Research
  state:
    view: all | findings
  actions:
    run()                                   # op:StartResearch
    send(text)                              # op:SendToResearch
    stop()                                  # op:StopResearch
    vote(iri, up | down)                    # op:VoteFinding
    star(iri)                               # op:KeepFinding
  layout: |
    ┌────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ [All | Findings] [Stop]                                        │
    ├────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ Goal                   │ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐            │
    │ Budget  Engines ▸      │ │Pick 1│ │Pick 2│ │ card │  masonry   │
    │ meters          [Run]  │ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘            │
    ├────────────────────────┤ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐                     │
    │ thread (ChatThread)    │ │ card │ │ card │                     │
    │ [follow-up…]    [➤]   │ └──────┘ └──────┘                     │
    └────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component ResultCard
  desc: >
    A masonry tile in plugin-commerce's ResultCard shape: the first photo, the star in the header's leading
    slot, the title and price (or key figure) in its centre, then the key facts as rows, the kind as a tag, the
    rating score and thumbs up and down. Built from a lighthouse entity by toCard, or from a kept Finding.
  props:
    card: CardModel
    starred: boolean
    score?: number
    vote?: up | down
  emits:
    onToggleStar()
    onVote(vote: up | down)
```

```mdl
component ResultArticle
  desc: >
    Companion to a Research (variant `result`): the selected result's detail. Its title, star, price, tags,
    score and thumbs; its link and photos; the agent's reason when it is a pick; the rating terms; every fact;
    where the facts came from (the graph's provenance); the extension sections already read; and "More about
    this", which reads another extension quickly or, for a deep one, starts a research session whose items (a
    menu's dishes) are listed by section; then its Relations, the result's one-hop graph. A kept Finding stands in
    when the session no longer has the result, and the graph when the node is no result of the session.
  props:
    research: Research
  actions:
    extend(extension, deep)                 # op:ExtendFinding
```

```mdl
component SubjectGraph
  desc: >
    The Research article's Graph mode, which an entity session ("everything about X") opens on: the session's
    subjects and what is around them as card nodes (photo, label, kind) laid out by a deterministic force-style
    layout, roots emphasised, edges coloured by predicate family with the predicate shown (CURIE prefix dimmed) on
    hover or selection, "+N more" on a capped node to fetch its neighbours, pan, zoom and fit. Selecting a node opens
    it in the result companion, which reads a node that is no result from the graph.
  props:
    graph: SubjectGraph
    selectedId?: string
```

```mdl
component TracePanel
  desc: >
    The Research article's Trace mode: the session's trajectory as a tree (input, agent turn, tool call, command,
    loads, extractions, model calls), each row with its time, a bar placing it on the session's timeline, its cost
    and what it yielded (pages, facts, results). Rows are coloured by what ran them (the LLM, System One, or no
    model) and interleaved in time; runs of System One calls are folded into one row.
  props:
    tree: ExplainNode
```

```mdl
component ModelPanel
  desc: >
    The session's rating model, behind the article toolbar's Rating model toggle: the score formula, then each term
    with its formula and the session's numbers (CURIE prefixes dimmed), its coverage and share, an on/off switch, a
    nudge and a weight slider; requirements with switches; reset. Adjustments re-rank at once and are saved to the
    session's overrides.
  props:
    model: RatingModel
    overrides?: RatingOverrides
```

```mdl
component LighthouseMeta
  desc: >
    A companion to a Lighthouse connection: lighthouse's plugins and what they contribute, its vocabulary
    (predicates with their meanings, synonyms and extractors, filterable), its issues with triage (comment, change
    status), and its storage (bytes by area, cache namespaces with clear, snapshot prune with a dry run first).
  props:
    connection: Connection
```

```mdl
component ResearchThread
  desc: >
    The session's trajectory as the assistant ChatThread, as lighthouse's own web UI renders it: prompts; one
    run row per narration, collapsed to the narration, its call and result counts, failures and time, and
    opened onto each call (tool, arguments, outcome, time, output or error) and the results it put into the
    graph as pills; the report as pick rows. A vote's feedback prompt reads as one line naming the voted
    results. A composer below sends follow-ups; a failed or stopped session ends with a Retry chip.
  props:
    messages: Message[]
    busy: boolean
  emits:
    onSend(text, model?)
```

## Services

```mdl
service LighthouseClient
  desc: >
    The lighthouse-api client, bound to one endpoint (server URL and API token): every request the plugin makes
    to lighthouse, and the session stream (Server-Sent Events read over fetch, so it can send the bearer
    token, resuming with Last-Event-ID). Hosts contribute it through the ClientFactory capability, matched by
    the connection's URL; the plugin contributes the HTTP one.
  loading: lazy
```

## Operations

The article computes the facts a Finding keeps (it holds the session's results); the operations write ECHO and
call lighthouse.

```mdl
op StartResearch
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.start
  desc: Creates the lighthouse session for a Research's goal, engines and budget preset, and records its run.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
  output: string                            # the run
  errors:
    ResearchGoalMissing: the Research has no goal
    LighthouseNotConnected: the Research names no connection
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op SendToResearch
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.send
  desc: A follow-up into the session, sent from composer; queued while a turn runs.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    text: string
    model?: string                          # "default" is the Retry path
  effects: [http]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op StopResearch
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.stop
  desc: Aborts the turn in flight; the session can be continued later.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
  effects: [http]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op SyncFindings
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.sync
  desc: >
    Appends to the Research's feed every pick that is not kept as a pick yet, by subject, with keptBy pick.
    The article runs it when the session reports.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    picks: FindingInput[]
  output: number                            # Findings appended
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op KeepFinding
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.setStarred
  desc: >
    Stars a result: the first time, copies it into the feed (with the graph's provenance) as keptBy person.
    Unstarring removes the star, never the entry.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    finding: FindingInput
    starred: boolean
  effects: [http, echo:write]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op VoteFinding
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.sendFeedback
  desc: Sends a thumbs up or down (or clear) on a result to lighthouse, which rebuilds the rating model.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    iri: string
    vote: up | down | clear
  effects: [http]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

```mdl
op ExtendFinding
  key: org.dxos.operation.lighthouse.readExtension
  desc: Reads one extension for one result; deep starts a child research session and returns its run.
  input:
    research: Ref<Research>
    iri: string
    extension: string
    deep?: boolean
  output: { child?: string }
  effects: [http]
  requires: [LighthouseClient]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Connection

  req F-1.1: The plugin registers a plugin-connector Connector for lighthouse with a credential form (server URL, default http://127.0.0.1:4319, and API token); the token is an AccessToken and the form checks it against the server's status before saving.
  req F-1.3: A connection that does not answer leaves the article readable: the Findings view shows the kept Findings, and the stream shows reconnecting.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Research

  req F-2.1: A Research is created from the space's create menu, with a goal and a budget preset (Quick, Standard, Deep); a space with one lighthouse connection gives the Research that connection.
  req F-2.2: Running it creates the lighthouse session and stores its run; the article streams it from then on.
  req F-2.3: The thread is steering only: results appear in the masonry, and the report's picks appear as pick rows in the thread and first in the masonry.
  req F-2.4: A follow-up sent from Composer is marked from composer; follow-ups from the CLI or lighthouse's own UI appear live.
  req F-2.5: The search engines the person checks are named in the session's goal; with none checked the agent chooses.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Findings in the space

  req F-3.1: When the session reports, its picks are appended to the feed as Findings with keptBy pick, once each.
  req F-3.2: Starring a result appends it as a Finding with keptBy person and stars it; unstarring removes the star, not the entry.
  req F-3.3: Findings are immutable; the feed is the Research's history of what was kept.
  req F-3.4: Members of the space see the Research and its Findings without a lighthouse connection of their own.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Ranking and facets

  req F-4.1: The masonry ranks by the session's rating model with the person's adjustments, as lighthouse's web UI does.
  req F-4.2: Votes are sent to lighthouse and shown at once, ahead of the stream.
  req F-4.4: Extensions that apply to a result are offered in its companion; a deep one starts a child session.
```

Not built yet: the desktop sidecar that runs the daemon as the default connection (F-1.2) and the assistant skill
(F-5).

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Offline Research
  given: a Research with kept Findings; its connection does not answer
  when: a member opens it and picks Findings
  then:
    - the masonry shows the Findings as cards
    - the meters show reconnecting
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Picks are kept once
  given: a Research whose session reported 8 picks, 3 of them already in the feed as picks
  when: SyncFindings runs
  then: 5 Findings are appended, with keptBy pick
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Research a goal from Composer
  desc: The round trip through the API, against a local lighthouse daemon.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3, F-3.2, F-4.2, F-4.4]
  status: passing            # 2026-10-28; autocue/research.mjs dry run against the live daemon, every step passed
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - a lighthouse daemon is running locally on http://127.0.0.1:4319, with its API token at hand (`lighthouse api token`)
    - plugin-lighthouse is enabled (it is not on by default) and the space has a Lighthouse connection
  before:
    - name: Connect lighthouse
      do: In Settings → Connections, add Lighthouse with the server URL and the API token.
      expect: the connection is saved; its test passes
  steps:
    - name: Open Composer
      do: Open Composer on the space.
      expect: the space's navtree is shown
    - name: Create a Research with a goal
      do: Create a Research named "Board game cafés", and write the goal "Board game cafés in Bangkok with a big game library" with the Quick budget.
      expect: the Research opens with the goal, Quick and an enabled Run button
    - name: Run it
      do: Press Run.
      expect: the thread shows the goal as the prompt and the agent's first tool calls; the meters count pages and cost
    - name: Watch results land
      do: Wait while the agent searches.
      expect: result cards appear in the masonry, with photos, prices or ratings, and scores once the agent writes a rating model
      note: A Quick session takes up to 5 minutes; the step passes when at least 3 cards are shown.
    - name: Open a result in the companion
      do: Click a result card.
      expect: the companion shows the result's facts, where they came from, and More about this
    - name: Star and vote
      do: Star the result in the companion, and thumbs-up another card.
      expect: the star is filled; the thumbs-up is pressed
    - name: Show the kept Findings
      do: Pick Findings in the toolbar.
      expect: the starred result is shown as a card marked Kept · starred
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Search for apartments in Warsaw, live
  desc: A live search with the Standard budget whose results are listings with photos, kept from the companion.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3, F-3.2, F-4.2, F-4.4]
  status: passing            # 2026-10-28; autocue/apartments.mjs against the live daemon, every step passed
  given:
    - QA-1's given and before: the plugin is enabled and the space has a Lighthouse connection
    - the daemon's otodom engine is configured; a run costs up to the Standard budget
  steps:
    - name: Create a Research with the goal and the Standard budget
      do: Create a Research named "Warsaw apartments", write the goal "2-room apartments for rent in central Warsaw (Śródmieście, Wola, Mokotów) under 6000 PLN total with a balcony, near metro" and pick the standard budget.
      expect: the budget reads 10 min · $0.50 · 40 pages; Run is enabled
    - name: Run it
      do: Press Run and wait while the agent searches.
      expect: the agent searches otodom; listing cards land in the masonry with their photos, price, size, rooms and district
    - name: Open a run row
      do: Open the run row that counts results.
      expect: its calls with arguments and time, then its results as pills
    - name: Open a listing in the companion
      do: Click a card with a photo.
      expect: the companion shows the photos, the facts, where these facts came from (extractor and page), and More about this
    - name: Read its move-in cost
      do: Press Read next to Move-in cost.
      expect: a Move-in cost section with the deposit, fees and move-in total, and the move-in extension among the sources
    - name: Star and vote, then Findings
      do: Star the listing in the companion, thumbs-up another card, and pick Findings.
      expect: the starred listing is shown as a card marked Kept · starred
```

```mdl
test QA-3: Everything about BlueYard
  desc: An entity session started elsewhere, opened in Composer: its graph, a portfolio company's facts, the investments as cards, the trace.
  actors: both
  status: passing            # 2026-10-28; autocue/blueyard.mjs against vc-blueyard-entity, every step passed
  given:
    - QA-1's given and before: the plugin is enabled and the space has a Lighthouse connection
    - the daemon holds the reported entity session vc-blueyard-entity (BlueYard, its team, funds and portfolio)
  steps:
    - name: Open the session
      do: Create a Research named "BlueYard" with Existing session "vc-blueyard-entity".
      expect: the Research opens on the Graph view, BlueYard's card at the centre with partners, funds and portfolio companies around it, people with photos and companies with logos
    - name: Open a portfolio company
      do: Click a portfolio company's card with a logo (IonQ, Privy, Protocol Labs or Castelion).
      expect: the companion shows its facts, where they came from (extractor, page, date), and its relations
    - name: Refocus on the company
      do: Double-click the company's card, then press Back to subjects.
      expect: the graph refocuses on the company's neighbourhood (about 30 cards); Back returns to BlueYard's graph
    - name: The investments as cards
      do: Pick Results in the toolbar.
      expect: the cards with pictures lead (Castelion, BlueYard, Corintis, Privy, Groq, IonQ…); cards without one show a type icon
    - name: The trace
      do: Pick Trace.
      expect: the session's turns, calls and page loads as rows with time and cost

test QA-4: Areas on the map
  desc: An apartment session opened in Composer, ranked by where its listings are: the map beside the cards, the location popover, the areas in the rating model, a circle drawn and deleted.
  actors: both
  status: passing            # 2026-10-29; autocue/geo.mjs against web-20261028-110009, every step passed
  given:
    - QA-1's given and before: the plugin is enabled and the space has a Lighthouse connection
    - the daemon holds the session web-20261028-110009 with the areas "Around Mokotów" (require) and "Mokotów" (prefer, 400 m)
  steps:
    - name: Open the session
      do: Create a Research named "Warsaw apartments" with Existing session "web-20261028-110009".
      expect: the Research opens on the Map, OSM tiles with attribution, pins coloured by score with clusters, unrated places as small grey markers, both areas drawn with their chips (name, Prefer/Require, soft edge, count inside, zoom, delete); cards outside the areas say "outside your areas"
    - name: Hover a card's location
      do: Hover the location row of the first card.
      expect: a popover with a small map, the pin and its precision ring, the address, and links to OpenStreetMap and Google Maps; Esc closes it
    - name: The areas in the rating model
      do: Open the Rating model.
      expect: the preferred area as a term marked yours, `s = inside(area "Mokotów") ? 1 : max(0, 1 − dist / 400 m)`, Edit on the map; the required area as a requirement with Prefer instead; each area a chip under its term or requirement with a prefer/require switch and a delete
    - name: Draw a circle near a point
      do: Pick Near a point, press on the map and drag out a radius.
      expect: a third area chip with its count inside; the cards re-rank; the areas are saved to the session through /v1
    - name: Delete it again
      do: Delete the new area's chip.
      expect: the session's areas are the two it had
    - name: Open a result
      do: Click a card.
      expect: the companion shows its location row with the popover, and "outside your areas" when it is

test QA-5: Filters and sort
  desc: The person's own filters and sort on a session's results, beside the agent's ranking: they cut the cards and the map's pins, keep and count unknowns, sort by any number, and are saved with the session.
  actors: both
  status: passing            # 2026-10-29; autocue/filters.mjs against web-20261028-110009, every step passed
  given:
    - QA-1's given and before: the plugin is enabled and the space has a Lighthouse connection
    - the daemon has /v1 GET|PUT /sessions/:run/view and holds web-20261028-110009 (123 results) with its rating model; its filters and sort are cleared first
  steps:
    - name: Open the panel
      do: Open the session as a Research and press Filters in the toolbar.
      expect: controls derived from the results — ranges with a histogram and min/max (total monthly cost, floor area, rooms), checkbox lists with counts (district), toggles; "N of M"; a Sort select
    - name: Cost and rooms
      do: Set the total monthly cost to at most 6000 and the rooms to at least 2.
      expect: fewer results; each range says "Include N without this"
    - name: Has a balcony
      do: Turn on Has a balcony (under More filters when not shown), untick Include … without this, tick it again.
      expect: known balconies only cut the list further; ticking it again keeps the unknowns
    - name: Sort by floor area
      do: Pick Floor area (m²) ↓ highest first.
      expect: 39 of 123, the cards largest first; the picks join the sorted list marked Pick #N; the map shows only the 39 kept
    - name: Chips
      do: Close the panel.
      expect: the filters as chips above the cards with "incl. N unknown", the sort chip and Clear all
    - name: Saved
      do: Reload.
      expect: the same chips and "39 of 123"

test QA-6: Search by image
  desc: An image search opened in Composer: the photo the person gave and what lighthouse read from it, how much each result looks like it, and attaching a photo to a follow-up.
  actors: both
  status: passing            # 2026-10-29; autocue/image.mjs against image-mizuno-bkk-2, every step passed
  given:
    - QA-1's given and before: the plugin is enabled and the space has a Lighthouse connection
    - the daemon holds the image session image-mizuno-bkk-2 (find a Mizuno SINCE.1906 top in central Bangkok)
  steps:
    - name: Open the session
      do: Create a Research named "Mizuno top" with Existing session "image-mizuno-bkk-2".
      expect: the thread's first input shows the photo, "Read: Mizuno long-sleeve football training top", the marks and printed text with their crops (logo, "SINCE.1906", crest "C A"; no face) and the queries it suggested
    - name: Visual match on cards
      do: Look at the result cards.
      expect: product results say "looks N% like your image" and a Visual match row naming the matched features
    - name: Attach to a follow-up
      do: Attach the photo in the composer, then remove it.
      expect: a thumbnail above the composer with a remove button; nothing is sent
```

## Open questions

- Web-only Composer users: a local daemon reached from the browser, a hosted lighthouse, or both.
- Whether every result should be kept automatically (larger spaces, offline-complete) rather than picks and
  the person's stars.
- plugin-commerce: its Provider templates could become a lighthouse extractor kind, with commerce searches run by
  lighthouse's runSearch; or this plugin replaces it.

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Composer is lighthouse's web UI: a Composer plugin reaches lighthouse through its API, while lighthouse's code stays in its own repository.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The plugin adds a Research object linked to one lighthouse session; its article is lighthouse's two-pane view (the assistant ChatThread steering on the left, the ranked masonry on the right) reading the session live from the API. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: Lighthouse's web UI is already built from the same DXOS components, so the view ports with its behavior intact.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The session's picks and the results a person keeps are copied into the space as immutable Findings in the Research's feed, with provenance; everything else is read live and not copied. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: Copies are what members without a connection see and what outlives the lighthouse workspace; copying every result (hundreds per session) would fill spaces with what nobody chose.
  rejected: Copying every result; copying nothing (a Research unreadable without the person's own lighthouse).
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The connection is a plugin-connector Integration with the API token as an AccessToken; on the desktop app a Tauri sidecar runs the lighthouse daemon and is the default connection. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: plugin-connector already stores credentials and renders the setup; plugin-claude's dx-agent is the precedent for a local server beside the desktop app.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The Research article follows plugin-commerce's Search: the left pane holds the goal, the budget preset (Quick, Standard, Deep), optionally the search engines (from listEngines, like commerce's provider checkboxes) and Run, with the session's steering thread under them; the right pane is the masonry of results in commerce's ResultCard style (image, title, price or key facts, star) ranked by the rating model, with thumbs; clicking a tile opens the detail in the companion pane: the entity's facts with provenance, its extension sections and "More about this" (quick read or research). Supersedes [D-2].
